 "upload": {
  "title": "October 2026 Broke the Record. Is 2026 Next? #shorts",
  "description": "Copernicus says October 2026 was the warmest October in its records, about 1.75°C above pre-industrial levels, and NOAA confirmed on November 12 that it was the warmest October since its records began in 1850, with a fifth straight monthly ocean-temperature record. Copernicus says 2026 is virtually certain to end above 1.5°C but most likely ranks second behind 2024.\n\nSources: Copernicus Climate Change Service (Nov 6 bulletin), NOAA NCEI (Nov 12), reported by AFP via RTE and CP24, Fox Weather and Yale Climate Connections (based on search-result excerpts). Warm areas on the map are illustrative.\n\n#climate #weather #copernicus #noaa #recordheat",
